  "body": "The Anything Else case of the Character Reference State discarded the\r\nampersand that had been consumed to enter the state. This led to e.g. in\r\nthe Data State, \"&\\*\" emitting only a \"*\" char token, when you'd expect\r\nboth a \"&\" and \"\\*\" char token.\r\n\r\nThis fix appends the & to the attribute value if it was consumed while\r\nconsuming an attribute value, or otherwise emits it as a character token.",
